  "summary_en": "Japan's Mobility Roadmap 2026, decided by the Digital Society Promotion Council, sets policy for commercialising Level 4 autonomous driving services. It reviews 2025 results (transport trading-house function, 13 priority regions) and outlines measures: end-to-end AI driving support, remote monitoring communications, cybersecurity, accident investigation, liability review and international standards.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Continue 'transport trading house' function and concentrated support for 13 priority commercialisation regions targeting Level 4 business by FY2027.",
   "Support E2E AI driving development: data ecosystem, compute, and safety evaluation methods.",
   "Build accident investigation system at Japan Transport Safety Board and re-examine liability rules for autonomous vehicles.",
   "Create national 'excellent certification' scheme for L2++ vehicles by 2026.",
   "Strengthen communications (5G SA, 5.9GHz V2X), cybersecurity and lead international standards at UN WP.29 and ISO."
